The array order is a distraction: the operation depends only on the multiset of values.

## Key observation

Write every value uniquely as

\[
A_i = b \cdot 2^k
\]

where \(b\) is odd and \(k=v_2(A_i)\), the number of trailing zero bits.

Merging two equal values gives

\[
b2^k+b2^k \longrightarrow b2^{k+1}.
\]

The odd part \(b\) never changes, so values with different odd parts can never interact.

For each odd part \(b\), imagine a binary counter whose bit \(k\) indicates whether one \(b2^k\) remains:

- inserting \(b2^k\) sets bit \(k\);
- if bit \(k\) was already set, the two copies merge, clearing bit \(k\) and carrying into bit \(k+1\);
- carries continue until an empty bit is found.

After all carries, every value occurs at most once. This state is canonical, and its number of set bits is the minimum number of remaining elements.

## Processing each prefix

Maintain a set of occupied exponents for every odd part.

When inserting \(b2^k\):

1. Initially the answer increases by \(1\).
2. While exponent \(k\) is already occupied:
   - remove it;
   - decrement the answer by \(1\), because a merge reduced the size;
   - increment \(k\).
3. Insert the first unoccupied exponent.

Although one insertion can cause many carries, the total number of carries is \(O(N)\): each carry decreases the maintained size by one, while each insertion increases it by only one.

Therefore, ordered sets give \(O(N\log N)\) total time per test data set and \(O(N)\) memory.

## C++17 implementation

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int T;
    cin >> T;

    while (T--) {
        int N;
        cin >> N;

        vector<long long> a(N);
        vector<long long> oddPart(N);
        vector<int> exponent(N);

        for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {
            cin >> a[i];

            long long x = a[i];
            int k = 0;

            while ((x & 1LL) == 0) {
                x >>= 1;
                ++k;
            }

            oddPart[i] = x;
            exponent[i] = k;
        }

        // Coordinate-compress the odd parts.
        unordered_map<long long, int> id;
        id.reserve(2 * N);
        id.max_load_factor(0.7);

        vector<set<int>> occupied;
        occupied.reserve(N);

        int currentSize = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {
            long long b = oddPart[i];
            int k = exponent[i];

            auto found = id.find(b);
            int group;

            if (found == id.end()) {
                group = (int)occupied.size();
                id[b] = group;
                occupied.emplace_back();
            } else {
                group = found->second;
            }

            set<int>& bits = occupied[group];

            // Add the new element before performing carries.
            ++currentSize;

            auto it = bits.lower_bound(k);

            // Carry through a consecutive run of occupied bits.
            while (it != bits.end() && *it == k) {
                it = bits.erase(it);
                --currentSize;
                ++k;
            }

            bits.insert(k);

            cout << currentSize << (i + 1 == N ? '\n' : ' ');
        }
    }

    return 0;
}
```

